# 15. AUDITED SUPPORT ACCESS – CRITICAL SECURITY MODULE

This is a particularly important feature.

A SaaS Super Admin must not have silent, unrestricted access to customer company data.

Create a dedicated audited support access system.

### Support access request

When a support agent needs to inspect a customer environment, require:

- Tenant.
- Support ticket reference.
- Business reason.
- Requested access scope.
- Requested duration.
- Data categories requested.
- Approver.

### Access levels

1. Tenant metadata only.
2. Read-only configuration support.
3. Limited operational diagnostics.
4. Explicitly approved sensitive-data access, only where justified and legally permitted.

Default to metadata-only or read-only access.

Sensitive data access must be exceptional.

### Approval workflow

Support agent submits request.

↓

Authorized approver reviews the reason and scope.

↓

Customer consent or other valid authorization is obtained when required by contract, law or policy.

↓

Time-limited access is granted.

↓

Every access and action is recorded.

↓

Access automatically expires.

### Support session interface

Show:
- Tenant.
- Support ticket.
- Access reason.
- Approved scope.
- Approver.
- Start time.
- Expiration time.
- Session status.

Provide an obvious banner whenever a support session is active.

Do not impersonate the tenant administrator silently.

Do not use shared credentials.

Do not bypass tenant RLS.

Do not allow unrestricted exports of sensitive customer records.

### Audit history

Record:
- Who requested access.
- Who approved it.
- Who entered the session.
- What tenant was accessed.
- Which resources were viewed.
- What changes were performed.
- When the session ended.
- Why the session ended.

Provide immediate session revocation.

This module must be designed as a security-first governance workflow, not as a hidden backdoor.

